# profiles/default.env — every knob the pipeline has, at its default value.
#
# This file is documentation that runs: `BLOG_PROFILE=default bin/suggest.sh`
# behaves exactly like `bin/suggest.sh`, because every line below repeats what
# lib/config.sh would have resolved anyway. It exists so a real profile can be
# written by copying it and changing three lines — and so there is one place
# that lists what is tunable at all.
#
# A profile states only its DELTAS. Everything it leaves out falls through to
# the defaults, and anything already in the environment outranks it:
#
#   MAX_NEW=3 BLOG_PROFILE=personas bin/suggest.sh    # MAX_NEW=3 wins
#
# Values are shell assignments: quote what has spaces, $BLOG_REPO_DIR works.

# --- models (experiment 1) -----------------------------------------------------
# Per stage, because the stages are different jobs. CLAUDE_MODEL still overrides
# both of the first two at once; the typo pass has never followed it.
CLEANUP_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
CURATE_MODEL=claude-opus-5
TYPO_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# --- prompts (experiment 2) -----------------------------------------------------
# PROMPTS_DIR is an OVERLAY: a directory that need only contain the prompt files
# it changes; everything else falls back to prompts/. That is the whole of a
# prompt experiment.
#   PROMPTS_DIR=$BLOG_REPO_DIR/eval/overlays/curator-terse
# Individual prompts can also be pinned outright:
#   SUGGEST_PROMPT=$BLOG_REPO_DIR/eval/overlays/x/suggest.md
PROMPTS_DIR=

# --- directives (experiment 3) --------------------------------------------------
# The third slot in the prompt assembly: instructions + style anchor + directive
# + input. A small free-text file saying something the shared prompt does not.
#   CLEANUP_DIRECTIVE=$BLOG_REPO_DIR/eval/directives/loose-cleanup.md
#   CURATE_DIRECTIVE=$BLOG_REPO_DIR/eval/directives/poe.md
CLEANUP_DIRECTIVE=
CURATE_DIRECTIVE=

# PERSONAS: a TSV of `name <TAB> directive-file` (paths relative to the TSV).
# When set, the generation step runs once per persona with MAX_NEW split between
# them, and every candidate is stamped with the persona that produced it — one
# pool, several voices, judged blind because the filename and body say nothing.
#   PERSONAS=$BLOG_REPO_DIR/eval/personas/two-authors.tsv
PERSONAS=

# --- the stitching gate (experiment 4) ------------------------------------------
VERBATIM_MIN=85
GLUE_MAX_WORDS=12
NEW_SLACK_EVERY=25
# How many words may be cut out of the MIDDLE of a sentence — the false start,
# the aside — with the result still grading as the author's sentence, and only
# when that sentence comes from a DICTATED note. Cutting a sentence's ends is
# already free for every source (a trimmed sentence is still a substring of its
# note). 0 disables the whole mechanism and is the default.
VOICE_TWEAK_GAP=0
# How much of a dictated sentence's wording a REWRITE must keep (word overlap,
# percent) to still count as his. This one permits real rewording, not just
# cuts — speech is first-draft thinking, and its sentences are often not the
# ones he would have written. The floor is what keeps a rewrite anchored to a
# specific thing he said instead of being free invention. 0 disables it.
VOICE_REWRITE_MIN=0
# enforce = a failing candidate is rejected (the pillar: posts are stitched, not
# written). report = classify but never reject, so a relaxed variant can be
# measured instead of being wiped out by its own gate. EXPERIMENTS ONLY — report
# mode is how the one non-negotiable property of this pipeline gets turned off.
GATE_MODE=enforce
# Annotate every GLUE/NEW sentence with its nearest corpus sentence and a word
# diff, in the provenance report. Forced on in report mode, where that
# annotation is the entire point of the run.
GATE_TRACE=0

# --- cleanup (experiment 5) -----------------------------------------------------
# A looser cleanup is a prompt in an overlay plus, if you want it, a directive.
# What it did is already measured: changes.diff per bundle, and the churn
# percentage in each bundle's meta.json.
STRUCTURE=0

# --- pool and corpus ------------------------------------------------------------
MAX_LONG=4
MAX_SHORT=8
MAX_NEW=8
TRASH_DAYS=14
REJECT_DAYS=30
CORPUS_MAX=150000
HISTORY_LINES=40
ARCHIVE_DAYS=14
REUSE_MIN_WORDS=6
REUSE_DROP_PCT=75

# --- typo pass ------------------------------------------------------------------
TYPO_FIX=1
TYPO_MIN_LEN=4
TYPO_MAX_PCT=5

# --- transcription --------------------------------------------------------------
WHISPER_MODEL=$BLOG_REPO_DIR/models/ggml-large-v3-q5_0.bin
WHISPER_LANG=auto
WHISPER_MARKS=1
WHISPER_CONF_LOW=0.40
WHISPER_CONF_VLOW=0.25
# WHISPER_THREADS is a performance knob (defaults to all cores) and is
# deliberately not part of the config fingerprint.

# --- retention ------------------------------------------------------------------
SYNC_KEEP_DAYS=14

# --- anonymization --------------------------------------------------------------
# NAME_SCAN=0 disables the name scout entirely. SELF_NAME, ALIASES and the
# reserve alias pools are settable too but are NOT part of the fingerprint:
# they are privacy configuration, not a variant, and one of them holds a real
# name that must never be printed by a command whose output lands in a log.
NAME_SCAN=1

# --- the tree -------------------------------------------------------------------
# BLOG_ROOT re-roots ALL data paths at once — the keystone of offline
# experiments (bin/ab.sh sets it per sandbox). Individual overrides exist too:
# BLOG_SYNC, BLOG_DRAFTS, BLOG_WORK, BLOG_LOGS, BLOG_PROMPTS, BLOG_VAULT,
# BLOG_POSTS, BLOG_ARCHIVE. Left unset here on purpose: a profile that pins the
# root would follow you into the live run.
